#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""locachy-nvidia: Arch Wiki DKMS NVIDIA driver manager (auto -> open -> 580xx -> off).

Detects installed NVIDIA GPUs via PCI sysfs + /usr/share/hwdata/pci.ids (with
lspci fallback) and classifies them against the Arch Wiki NVIDIA GPU family
table so driver branch selection works automatically without per-machine rules:

  1. auto   Automatically select and install the recommended DKMS branch for the
            detected GPU family (Blackwell+ -> open; Ada/Ampere/Turing -> open;
            Volta/Pascal/Maxwell -> 580xx; Kepler and older -> unsupported/off).
  2. open   (new, Arch Wiki default for Turing RTX 20+ / Ampere / Ada / Blackwell+):
            nvidia-open-dkms + nvidia-utils + dkms + active kernel headers
            (GSP-RM firmware is mandatory on open kernel modules; works with
            Zagitta/gpu-unlock on branch 615+ where NVreg_GpuInitOnProbe defaults
            back to probe-time AUTO).
  3. 580xx  (legacy proprietary 580xx: Maxwell/Pascal/Volta, and manual fallback
            for Turing/Ampere/Ada laptops needing GSP off via
            NVreg_EnableGpuFirmware=0 for troubleshooting):
            nvidia-580xx-dkms + nvidia-580xx-utils + dkms + active kernel headers.
  4. off    Remove NVIDIA driver packages and modprobe drop-in.

Commands:
  locachy-nvidia status [--json | --tsv]
  locachy-nvidia set auto|open|580xx|off [--force]
  locachy-nvidia gsp auto|off|on
  locachy-nvidia sync-dropin
"""
